akes at most 3 attempts in total, waiting `backoff * 2**attempt` seconds between them: 0.5s, then 1s by default. If the third attempt also gets a 503, that error is raised. Any other HTTP error is raised straight away without retrying.\n\n- **New setting:** `__init__` takes a new `backoff=0.5` parameter, and the attempt limit is the class attribute `MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3`.\n- **Connection cleanup:** the 503 response is closed before each retry so the connection isn't left open.\n\nI tested it against a real local HTTP server with `backoff=0.01`. The repo has no test suite, so I didn't add one.\n\n| Server behaviour | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| 200 straight away | data returned | 1 |\n| 503, 503, then 200 | data returned | 3 |\n| 503 every time | `HTTPError 503` raised | 3 |\n| 500 | `HTTPError 500` raised | 1 |\n\nNetwork errors such as timeouts or refused connections (`URLError`) are not retried, because you only asked for 503.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 0, "requests_cache_write": 178165, "requests_cost_usd": 0.923993, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1656, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial2", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 3, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T04:36:23.942921+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 23.399, "t_checker_s": 1.882, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1668, "tokens_cache_read": 0, "tokens_cache_write": 178165, "tokens_fresh": 1668, "tokens